id: pm-web-5sx6
title: Inspect cited evidence freshness and affected criteria
description: "Present pm-evidence facts for one authorized item in an item panel and the same compact SDK, CLI and HTTP response. Source roots and allowed file identities are selected by the server. No source resolution or review judgment is reimplemented."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-web#278"
created_at: "2026-10-29T04:15:12.821Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T07:15:06.643Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Editing one allowed source updates only affected displayed evidence; A viewer cannot trigger schema writes or access another project sources; Unsupported backend mutation support is clearly refused; UI and compact machine endpoint have identical meaning; source freshness never claims completion
blocked_by: pm-web-cnhi
blocked_reason: Current unretained JSON fragments require a supported pm-evidence resolver API; sibling-repository scope decision is pending.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-web-cnhi,blocked_by,"2026-10-29T07:10:57.690Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:blocked_by",detected
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T04:15:55.586Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against the installed CLI public SDK declarations and current pm-evidence, pm-review and pm-web agent context/contract/permission features. Core owns item reads, history, schemas and output shaping; pm-evidence owns exact fragment resolution, freshness and criterionFacts; pm-review owns judgments; existing web views carry receipts. This feature only presents authorized pm-evidence facts. Acceptance: changing one allowed source changes only its evidence rows; viewer inspection performs no schema writes and cannot select other project sources; mutation attempts return typed remedies; UI, SDK, CLI and compact endpoint share one response. No import/export/sync, journal, status interpretation, idempotency key or mutable coordination state is introduced. Read-only observations re-read SDK state before returning; no transaction isolation is claimed (upstream #1620)."
  "2026-10-29T04:26:54.370Z",codex-agent,"Implemented one read-only fact page through pm-evidence check(record:false), criterionFacts, producer citation schemas/replay and guarded file/json adapters. Host-injected SDK clients use noExtensions; linked project sources only, network-only UI/SW, no schema setup or mutation dispatch. Genuine PostgreSQL HTTP validation passed: viewers read identical SDK facts, methods refuse 405 unsupported, untrusted scope/query fields refuse 400, other projects and revoked users refuse 404, settings/history unchanged. Desktop/mobile browser assertions passed for selective source refresh and stale-row clearing; adjusting probe teardown to use the harness-owned pool lifecycle. Immutable public-main tracker validation: 190/190 items, zero refusals, zero citation rows (explicit corpus limitation), maximum 107 estimated tokens, 411 read-only source files, 72427 ms, source hash unchanged. No isolation guarantee: native item re-read detects concurrent changes; the final-read and authorization-to-response windows remain documented."
  "2026-10-29T04:41:55.761Z",codex-agent,"Verified: pm test --run --progress --timeout 1200 passed both linked commands (7 focused tests including 500 seeded sequences/2000 source operations, plus 1 genuine PostgreSQL/HTTP/CLI test). Result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment records the successful receipts without changing policy. Additional schema fuzz passed 1000 generated input/output envelopes and extreme/nonfinite/sparse cases. Shared permission-impact command regression passed 3 tests. Browser probe passed at 1440 and 390 pixels with one changed source row, one unchanged row, zero stale rows after refusal and no overflow. Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: forcing inspectEvidence freshness to current fails the source-edit regression (current versus changed); the package implementation passes afterward. Final read-only public corpus measurement: 190/190 items, zero refusals/citations/source reads, max 120 estimated tokens, 411 immutable source files unchanged, 290634 ms; zero citations is an explicit limitation, not evidence of citation coverage. Build/typechecks, lint, docstrings (203 files, 931 declarations) and duplication (zero clones) pass. Packed launcher matrix and full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to exact-head CI at unchanged thresholds. Overlap reconfirmed: CLI freshness declarations describe derived projections/discovery; pm-context freshness/evidence packing handles packet sources; pm-review coverage handles judgments; this UI consumes pm-evidence facts only. No out-of-scope implementation or deployment."
  "2026-10-29T04:49:12.713Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/278 . Follow-up: malformed explicit project UUIDs now return invalid_input before network access rather than unavailable; the targeted SDK/CLI refusal test passes and server/test typechecks pass. The pm item is tagged gh:unbraind/pm-web#278 for exact sync identity. The implementation claim is released again after this correction. Fresh CI at the new head is required; the PR checks and final report carry the exact full npm/Bun gate receipt. No source-verification or storage behavior changed."
  "2026-10-29T05:13:03.828Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility correction and behavioral proof: a native project file link with the valid leading ./ alias incorrectly produced unknown/boundary. The source-policy regression failed with only the existing publicSource function (unknown versus current), then passed after normalizing the producer-supported alias before policy checks. Selective source edit, malformed-record/symlink boundaries and legacy/JSON/unlinked-source tests all pass (3/3); server/test typechecks pass. This preserves old native links and keeps traversal, hidden configuration and unlinked sources refused. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40820000516 was still running npm gates on Node 22/26 with Bun pending at the previous head; that is pending/superseded evidence, not final-head approval. The next head requires fresh full npm/Bun CI; remaining test counts and run URL are reported in the PR and final handoff. Do not close this item before independent verification."
  "2026-10-29T05:20:26.897Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40820000516 on the superseded head measured 875 tests: 871 passed, 4 failed, 0 skipped/canceled. The four failures were the registration count (14 expected versus 15 including web evidence) and three browser recovery fixture realms lacking the new evidence invalidation hook. Updated the explicit command/flag contract and the isolated callback observer to assert evidence invalidation while retaining cursor/reconnection assertions. All six targeted registration/recovery tests now pass, including through pm test --only-last --run --progress; test typecheck passes. These are fixture integrations, not waived failures or lowered gates. Full npm/Bun release gates and packed acceptance remain required at the new head. The queued/in-progress rerun and exact missing counts are linked from PR 278 and the final handoff; no final-head full-gate approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-29T05:52:19.288Z",codex-agent,"Re-review repair scope: invariant 1 is authorization of the actual opened source object, including final targets and aliases, before reading or emitting any bytes; lexical linked-path checks alone are insufficient. Invariant 2 is independence of current-source resolution from retention of the historical cited fragment; current file/JSON fragments must be rendered from the same verified snapshot using pm-evidence resolution. Audited shared service adapters, HTTP route, SDK client, CLI command, UI renderer, JSON/TOON serialization, non-git fixtures and packed consumers. No inline reviewer findings or non-blocking code findings are published on the PR beyond the two orchestrator blockers; quota/disabled review notices are not approval. Branch is clean and origin/main is already an ancestor (4 ahead, 0 behind), so no merge is needed. The queue forbids sub-agents; independent boundary and bypass review passes will be performed directly. Installed pm-evidence public exports have no read-only fragment resolver/current text option; upstream public declarations and issues were checked. Requested narrow sibling-export authorization while implementing descriptor-based source policy in pm-web."
  "2026-10-29T06:37:48.680Z",codex-agent,"Opened-object repair now checks the canonical target and the opened file descriptor before bytes are read, refuses private/external aliases and multiply linked files, and checks descriptor/path identity and revision again before publication. Adversarial real-SDK plain-tracker tests passed all 40 provider/retention/private-alias combinations plus four deterministic directory-swap boundaries, with safe direct/chained/directory aliases as positive controls. The genuine PostgreSQL viewer route, SDK and CLI JSON/TOON regression passed (1 test), including retained private-alias redaction and unchanged schema/history. Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: replacing only readApprovedEvidence with the previous public fileAdapter reader makes the 40-case private-alias regression fail (boundary expected); the reviewed checkout was never modified by the mutant. Whole-package file-read audit found no other viewer-controlled project-source byte reader: remaining readers consume fixed package/static files, local process/config files or public fleet manifests. Current JSON fragment regression separately fails all five exact raw-span cases (escaped pointer, large integer, nonfinite JSON exponent, escaped string, prototype-named member and root selection) because current text incorrectly uses the absent original. The needed public pm-evidence signature is resolveFragment(text, descriptor): Fragment; it exists internally but is absent from root exports. Public SDK declarations and upstream issues were checked; sibling API authorization is pending. No workaround or weakened test is used."
  "2026-10-29T06:48:52.400Z",codex-agent,"Linked security regression was executed with pm test --only-last --run --progress --timeout 600: 5 tests, 4 passed and the known live-JSON regression failed, with no skips or cancellations. Existing project policy disables automatic test-result persistence; this comment preserves the failure rather than changing policy. Follow-up pm-web-cnhi records the exact supported-SDK capability needed for blocker 2. npm and Bun full release gates are running serially at one test worker, without inherited credentials; no green gate or zero-open-findings claim is made."
  "2026-10-29T07:01:40.386Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed four npm/Bun current/minimum host scenarios and eight launchers, including installed-server SDK private-alias refusals in every scenario. A final reserved-name case-folding correction and must-allow/must-refuse table were added; packed acceptance is being repeated against the final generated artifact. Additional reader tests passed size, cancellation, permissions, source-write and hardlink-insertion refusal controls at all four test boundaries. Full npm release validation has passed typechecks, lint, duplication and docstrings; two unrelated catalog-install tests have failed (a timeout and a subsequent install refusal). The gate is continuing to preserve complete results; no failures or tests are waived."
  "2026-10-29T07:05:31.828Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the prior progress note: the original host-resource instruction requires targeted local checks and CI for full npm/Bun gates. The local full-gate attempt was canceled during the 500-sequence test after 140 individual passes, two catalog-install failures and no complete count; those partial observations are NOT gate approval. Its owned process tree was stopped. Bun local full validation was not started. Full release verification remains the PR CI responsibility and cannot be green while the retained live-JSON regression is unresolved. The published pm-evidence API gap and pending sibling-scope decision are preserved in pm-web-cnhi; no private SDK import, fabricated citation state, scratch schema write or duplicate resolver was introduced."
  "2026-10-29T07:11:12.609Z",codex-agent,"Final focused security rerun through pm test --only-last --run --progress --timeout 600: 6 tests, 5 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped/canceled. The passing cases cover the shared reserved-name policy, 40 forbidden alias/provider/retention cases with no Git executable, safe aliases, every reader race barrier, bounds/permissions/cancellation and retained historical public bytes after source removal. The sole failing case is the five exact live JSON fragments without retention, intentionally kept as a failing regression for blocker 2 and linked from pm-web-cnhi. Typechecks, lint, duplication and docstrings passed before the canceled local full attempt. No SDK functionality was cloned or imported privately. Item remains unfinished and blocked on pm-web-cnhi; the claim will be released with the repair commit."
  "2026-10-29T07:14:50.361Z",codex-agent,"Final packed npm/Bun acceptance passed all 4 current/minimum host scenarios and all 8 launcher probes against one tarball, SHA256 2a65e1dcbb689576c7f503c0abac3f8b2def188057fd5abce66c542470f0be11. Each installed server SDK refused the synthetic private alias with null cited/current fragments. Broader replay-independence regression also ran through pm test: the additional test fails across an 18-case lines/headings/JSON matrix with current/changed sources and absent/valid/corrupt retained originals; native item state read back through the SDK is unchanged. Across the two focused invocations there are 7 distinct tests: 5 pass and 2 fail on blocker 2, with no skipped tests. The approved-source boundary repair and its behavioral revert proof are complete; current-fragment class closure is not complete. Prior real-data measurement remains 190/190 public items, zero citation/source reads, 411 immutable files unchanged; its zero-citation corpus limitation remains explicit. PR 278 will carry final-head CI receipts; no merge/release or readiness claim is made while this blocker remains."
